A||||12||kslish||"Fiero Fanatics" in Automobile Mag.||||8||
Z||000000||kslish||12-05-2000||01:17 AM||||Anyone remember the uproar over a certain article in Automobile Magazine a few months back?  (see these links if you need to refresh your memory):<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003585.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003585.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003713.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003713.html</A> <P>Here is the magazines reply to the Fiero community and our many letters and e-mails sent in to the magazine.  This reply is published in their Jan. 2001 issue.<P>-----------------------<P>It takes all kinds<P>Editor emeritus David E. Davis, Jr., touched a nerve with his October American Driver column, in which he looks back on the brief life span of the Pontiac Fiero and the curious community of Fiero collectors.  Letters poured in from enthusiasts across North America, prompted by discussions about the article on various enthusiast Web sites, message boards, and mailing lists. <P>Some irate letter writers questioned David E.'s qualifications as a journalist, perhaps unaware of his forty-plus years in the field: Michael Schaefer asked us to "promptly have an experienced automotive writer print a full-page apology."  He then told us to "go to hell."  Hmph.<P>Others simply couldn't stomach reading anything negative about their cars.  "lf you have an opinion that is positive, then by all means state it in your magazine.  But if you have a negative opinion or a bashing type of article, keep it to yourself, or leave the automotive writing business altogether," wrote Scott R. Lawrence.  We can't help but think that this would be a pretty boring magazine if we actually followed that advice, but hey, that's his opinion, and he's welcome to it.<P>Numerous enthusiasts wrote extolling the virtues af their Fieros and described their cars and the modifications they had made to them in detail, Marvin Lee, who with his son owns four Fiero GTs, blamed it on genetics.  "Someday, researchers will isolate the gene that compels us to appreciate a rustproof plastic body, mid-engine arrangement, and a cast iron, snarly V-6.  The gene may also be responsible for other eccentric behavior, such as choosing Harley over Honda, brunette instead of blonde, and decaf versus regular."<P>William F. Spohn chose to take the article with a grain of salt, writing: "I guess Mr. Davis must be still ducking the incoming, no doubt largely intemperate, responses from young Fiero advocates everywhere to his recent, less than laudatory editorial mention of the car in his column.. . . I know from reading other material written by Mr. Davis that the juices still flow and that he is capable of enjoying many a car.  I discount a portion of his disdain for the Fiero as simple editorial hyperbole.  Still, I commend the model to him for a second look.  Perhaps, on longer acquaintance, the car will still fail to impress, but it at least deserves a chance.  In the meantime, I wouldn't open any packages addressed with crayons or felt pens, without giving them the old stethoscope test."  Sounds like good advice.<P>Jonathan Pennypacker from North Carolina gets the last word: "David's ribbing of his friend Charlie Hughes sounds a lot like my grandfather's ribbing of my love for Fieros.  I always smile and say this: 'Fiero: If I have to explain it, you'll never understand.' "<P>---------------------<P><BR>I'm not sure if the above article is suppossed to be an apology or not, but at least it wasn't as harsh as the original article.  Still ticks me off a little that it was obviosly written by the editor instead of David E. Davis, Jr. writing a reply himself.  <P>Ken S.<BR>Secretary, Western PA Fiero Club <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Homicidal||12-05-2000||04:45 AM||||Two words:<P>@SS HOLE.<P>Doesn't he realize the reason he touched a nerve is he basically ripped on our hobby?  I would love to find what he does for fun and then redicule it in a nation wide magazine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||12-05-2000||09:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Others simply couldn't stomach reading anything negative about their cars. "lf you have an opinion that is positive, then by all means state it in your magazine.  But if you have a negative opinion or a bashing type of article, keep it to yourself, or leave the automotive writing business altogether," wrote Scott R. Lawrence. <B>We can't help but think that this would be a pretty boring magazine if we actually followed that advice, but hey, that's his opinion, and he's welcome to it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh oh, I can't wait for next months Automobile Magazine!!!  Hopefully they will write an article bashing the Ford Pinto!  Whoo hoo!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000003||DJRice||12-05-2000||09:31 AM||||I emailed the mag when that article came out and told them that Mr. Davis wouldnt know driving exictement if it popped him across the face.  I also suggested that he hop in his personal car, put on his leather driving gloves, and go ask the masses: "Pardon me, would you have any grey poupon"<P>Looking back, thats kind of a silly comment to make, but his article really pi$$ed me off.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000004||PearlBlueSoul||12-05-2000||02:54 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">Holey moley! that looks nearly EXACLTY like what the MR2 bbs was lookin like when that site was found.  <P>For those who can, Relate that to us, and that's how we felt.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||4
Z||000005||Black88GT||12-05-2000||03:22 PM||||But Pearl, we were bashed in a magazine sold all over the U.S. by a guy who apparently has (or had anyway) credentials.<P>You were bashed by some half @ss website written by some 15 yr. old punk who probably doesn't even own a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
