Z||000007||fropuff||12-05-2000||05:54 PM||||Good job, Mike Shaefer!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000008||gixxer||12-05-2000||06:55 PM||||Davis's editorial sounded like he was peeved. He is probably the only person in his "circle" that doesn't like Fieros. <BR>Road and Track liked the first'84.<BR>Motor Trend liked the '88. <BR>Charlie Hughs, who no doubt, has vastly more insider credibility in the automotive world, likes Fieros. What better way to get the last laugh than to write a snippy, sneering editorial? <BR>What qualifications does it require to be an automotive journalist nowadays? <BR>From reading that issue of Automobile, I would say; no automotive related knowledge is necessary, only a flair for the kings english.<BR>OW! (fell off the soapbox) ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DavidHenshaw||12-05-2000||10:39 PM||||I guess it is true that the Fiero is a somewhat quirky car and to love it like many of us do is a little quirky as well. In its defense it wasn't designed to be all things to all people.<P>Early models were supposed to be economical and sporty and they were. The later V6's were designed to be more sporty and they were, all of this on a beer budget. There have been numerous offerings from the industry with similar ambitions which fell flat on their faces. As for the quirkiness of Fiero lovers I don't think we can hold a candle to the people who build ultralight aircraft and then actually fly them.<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fformula88||12-05-2000||10:44 PM||||Forget what the article said within it.  We are now well into the '01 model year, a good 13 model years after the passing of our beloved Fiero.  Despite those 13 years, a well respected national automotive publication that basically focuses on new model cars has written dedicated articles to the Fiero in not just one, but TWO issues!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  I know they bashed it, and the reply above isn't exactly taking it back.  However, it sure says something about the Fiero that this much attention is being paid to it!  99% of 1980's cars will never be mentioned in a magazine like that again.  Not a blurb, much less two whole pieces!<P>That in itself is a compliment to the Fiero.  Even if Davis felt it was bad, he at least felt it was so bad to dedicate three pages to it.  He was a jerk to say what he did, and deserves all the criticism we can muster.  But deep down, its not all that bad.  People with high visibility are still talking about the Fiero!  Now, only if we could get Motortrend to write an article on the Fiero... they still speak highly of it!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||12-06-2000||01:48 AM||||I'm so disappointed that they didn't accept my challenge. For those who didn't know they said that the Fiero had "station wagon handling" So I challenged them on a closed race course, Any American made station wagon vs. my 86 Fiero. Never heard a response.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000012||WKDFIRO||12-06-2000||06:37 AM||||For our newsletter, I wrote up an article taking Davis' article apart and wondering just how much of a snob this guy can be. The specs come from various magazines and websites as well as MR-2 websites.<BR>    I would be more than happy to e-mail this to anyone if they would like to put it into their newsletters or just to have for themselves. Its in a Word Document (pictures and everything!) It may not make it onto the pages of Automobile Magazine (HA!) but it might just prove for good reading for any who are interested.<P>Just e-mail me!||||reg||2
